sentences.l:
A body wasted, and a heart wounded, * and tears upon the cheeks flowing;
and a beloved hard in fault-finding, but * whatever the fair-one does (is) fair.
O son of my uncle, you have filled with longing my heart; * my eye, from the tears, is sore.

sentences.i:
A wasted body and a wounded heart, * and tears that stream across the cheeks;
a loved one quick to find fault — and yet * whatever the beautiful do is beautiful.
Cousin, you have filled my heart with longing; * my eyes are raw with weeping.
